pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Truth: UNSATISFIABLE. The row is `-1 x1 >= 9223372036854775807`; the largest
% attainable left-hand side is 0, so no assignment satisfies it.
% Unfixed: normalizing flips `-1 x1` to `1 ~x1` and raises the degree to 2^63,
% which wraps to i64::MIN, storing the infeasible row as trivially true; the
% checker then accepts `conclusion SAT : x1`.
f 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT : x1 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
